Run the commands from the checkout in the
[ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/user-guide/quickstart')).

```=html
<div class="weights-workspaces">
  <section class="weights-workspace" aria-labelledby="inspect-model-weights">
    <h2 id="inspect-model-weights">Inspect weights</h2>
    <p>Read tensor names, shapes, data types and sizes from Safetensors metadata.</p>

    <fieldset class="command-tabs weights-source-tabs">
      <legend>Weight source</legend>
      <label id="inspect-a-local-checkpoint" class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="weights-source" value="local" aria-controls="weights-source-local" checked><span>Local</span></label>
      <label id="inspect-a-remote-checkpoint" class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="weights-source" value="hugging-face" aria-controls="weights-source-hugging-face"><span>Hugging Face</span></label>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="weights-source-content">
      <div id="weights-source-local" class="weights-source-panel" role="group" aria-labelledby="inspect-a-local-checkpoint">
        <p>Replace the example path with the absolute path to your weights.</p>
        <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy local weights inspection command">bazel run //examples/io:playground -- safetensors \
  "${HOME}/models/LiquidAI/LFM2-350M/model.safetensors"</code></pre>
        <p>For sharded weights, pass <code>model.safetensors.index.json</code> and keep the shards beside it. A model directory also works when it contains a <a href="https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/zml/safetensors.zig#L597-L615">recognized entry point</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="weights-source-hugging-face" class="weights-source-panel" role="group" aria-labelledby="inspect-a-remote-checkpoint">
        <p>List the files with <code>ls</code>, then inspect the file URI. The example pins a revision of <a href="https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/LFM2-350M/tree/f37d3f5c8c5484bc01dad379a595cf4c68c4e70e">LiquidAI/LFM2-350M</a>.</p>
        <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy Hugging Face weights inspection commands">model_uri='hf://LiquidAI/LFM2-350M@f37d3f5c8c5484bc01dad379a595cf4c68c4e70e'
bazel run //examples/io:playground -- ls "$model_uri"
bazel run //examples/io:playground -- safetensors "$model_uri/model.safetensors"</code></pre>
        <p>Omit <code>@revision</code> to use <code>main</code>. For gated repositories, request access and set <code>HF_TOKEN</code>. The playground also accepts <code>s3://</code> and <code>gs://</code>. See <a href="../../cli-reference/environment-variables/#model-storage-and-credentials">Environment variables</a> for storage credentials.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="weights-metadata">
      <figcaption>Illustrative metadata</figcaption>
      <dl>
        <dt>Name</dt><dd><code>projection.weight</code></dd>
        <dt>Shape</dt><dd>2 × 3</dd>
        <dt>Data type</dt><dd><code>f32</code></dd>
        <dt>Size</dt><dd>24 bytes</dd>
      </dl>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="weights-workspace" aria-labelledby="load-weights-for-execution">
    <h2 id="load-weights-for-execution">Load weights for execution</h2>
    <p>Check transfer to the selected backend with a small local weights file.</p>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy local weights transfer command">bazel run //examples/io:playground -- load \
  "${HOME}/models/LiquidAI/LFM2-350M/model.safetensors" replicated</code></pre>
    <p><code>replicated</code> places a full copy on each logical device. Allow memory for the copies and transfer buffers. The <a href="https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/examples/io/main.zig#L153-L222">load command</a> measures transfer time and bytes loaded, then releases the buffers.</p>

    <h3 id="loading-in-your-application">Loading in your application</h3>
    <ol class="weights-lifecycle">
      <li><strong><code>loader.load(…)</code></strong> Keep the loader, model, registry, store, destination buffers and platform alive during transfer.</li>
      <li><strong><code>loader.await(io)</code></strong> Wait for transfer before binding the buffers to the executable.</li>
      <li><strong><code>Buffer.deinit()</code></strong> The caller releases each weight buffer after its last use, before releasing the platform.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</div>
```

# [Load weights and run MNIST]($heading.id('load-weights-and-run-mnist'))

Run the MNIST example to see ZML load pretrained model weights and classify a
digit. Its Bazel target supplies the weights and sample dataset.

```sh
bazel run //examples/mnist
```

The [MNIST source](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/examples/mnist/mnist.zig#L17-L122)
opens a `TensorRegistry` and creates a `TensorStore` that borrows that registry
and the platform's replicated mesh. The model uses a view with prefix `fc1`
to create symbolic tensors bound to `fc1.weight` and `fc1.bias`. For example,
`store.view().withPrefix("fc1").createReplicatedTensor("weight", .{ .d_out, .d })`
reads the shape of `fc1.weight` from the model file and tags the matrix's two axes.

After compiling `forward`, the example fills a buffer structure that mirrors
the model. Here is the loading sequence inside `Mnist.load`, with `self` as
the model and `store` as a pointer to its tensor store.

```zig
var buffers = try zml.mem.bufferize(allocator, Mnist, self);
errdefer unloadBuffers(&buffers);

var loader: zml.io.Loader = try .init(allocator, platform, .default);
defer loader.deinit();

try loader.load(io, Mnist, self, &buffers, store, .{});
try loader.await(io);
return buffers;
```

After `await`, bind the loaded buffers and the input buffer with
[`args.set`]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/write-your-first-model').ref('compile-and-call-the-layer')).
The caller owns the returned `zml.Bufferized(Mnist)` and releases its weight
buffers with `Mnist.unloadBuffers`.

The walkthrough follows the pinned source. Execution checks are pending.
